                  "When would you use XML-style tags instead of JSON?",
                solution:
                  "<p>When the output is mostly prose with a little structure. JSON strings require escaping every quote, newline and backslash inside them, and long free-text values are exactly where models slip up — one unescaped quote inside a three-paragraph answer breaks the whole object. XML-style tags have no escaping problem, models follow them very reliably, and they stream gracefully because a partially-received tagged document is still readable. So for a RAG answer with citations, or an explanation with a structured summary attached, tags are frequently the better choice. Conversely, JSON is right when the output is mostly fields consumed by code. And for pure classification, neither — just return the enum value, since a whole JSON envelope is overhead for one word.</p>",
