                  "What is tool result bloat and why does it kill agents?",
                solution:
                  "<p>An agent calls a tool that returns a large payload — fifty thousand tokens of JSON from a database query or an API — and the result is appended verbatim to the conversation. Three tool calls later the context is full of API responses and the original task has been squeezed out, so the agent loses track of what it was doing. It is the single most common way agents fail, and it is entirely preventable. The fix is to never append a raw tool result: cap it at a token limit, and when it exceeds that, compress deliberately — return a count plus the most relevant few items rather than the whole array, or summarise free text <em>with the task in mind</em> so the summary keeps what this specific task needs. Save the full output to a scratchpad and return a reference, so the data still exists and is retrievable but is not crowding the window.</p>",
