                solution: `<p><strong>Stable content first, variable content last.</strong> Caching matches on a prefix and the match must be exact character for character, so the moment the text differs, caching stops applying from that point onward. That gives you a fixed prompt layout:</p>
             <pre><code className="language-text">
  system prompt          stable
  tool definitions       stable
  few-shot examples      stable
  [ CACHE BREAKPOINT ]
  conversation history   grows at the end
  retrieved chunks       varies per request
  user question          varies per request
             </code></pre>
             <p>Put one variable character at the top and you have cached nothing — and crucially, the system still works perfectly. Nothing errors, no test fails; you discover it on the invoice. That silent-failure property is what makes this worth designing for deliberately rather than fixing later.</p>`,
