                solution: `<p><strong>Ask questions before drawing anything.</strong> This is where candidates lose the most points. I would ask: what document types and formats? Do all users see all documents, or is there a permission model? What latency is acceptable? How often does content change, and how fresh must answers be? Any compliance or data-residency constraints? And what does success look like — what does a good answer mean to them?</p>
             <p>Then: state that there are two pipelines and separate them; walk indexing, naming what breaks at each stage; walk the query path with rough latencies; volunteer the evaluation story unprompted, with retrieval and generation measured separately; and close with what I would build first and what I would defer. That last part matters — showing prioritisation beats showing completeness, because a real project has a first two weeks.</p>`,
