             <p><strong>Wrong-but-confident</strong> is the hard half, and it is the pattern's most dangerous failure mode. A worker that misunderstood its subtask returns a fluent, plausible summary and the supervisor has no way to know. Mitigations: require <strong>sources</strong> in the output schema so claims are checkable; require a <strong>confidence</strong> score so weak findings can be discounted; have the supervisor flag conflicts between workers rather than silently picking one; and for high-stakes work, a <strong>critic</strong> with a clean context reviewing the synthesis.</p>
