             <p>I would say no, for five reasons. <strong>I can name every step before seeing the invoice</strong> — extract, validate, match, route, post. If I can draw the flowchart, I build the flowchart. <strong>The numbers are not close</strong>: two model calls at about 1.5 seconds and roughly £20 a day, versus four to nine calls at about eight seconds and roughly £150 a day, for the same output. <strong>Finance needs the same invoice to process the same way every time.</strong> <strong>I can test a pipeline properly</strong> — 500 labelled invoices, compare field by field, block the release on a regression. And <strong>debugging</strong> is one function and one test, not a trajectory.</p>
