             <p>What offline cannot tell me: <strong>what people actually ask</strong> — my set is questions I imagined, and real ones are shorter, vaguer and often about things I never covered. <strong>The real mix</strong> — my set is balanced on purpose, real traffic is 70% one boring category. Whether anyone finds it <strong>useful</strong>, as opposed to accurate. Speed and cost under real load. And <strong>the tail</strong> — the 1% of strange inputs that cause most incidents.</p>
