                  "Do apps in a monorepo share dependency versions?",
                solution:
                  "<p>Yes &mdash; there is one <code>package.json</code> and one <code>node_modules</code>, so every app uses the same version of every package.</p><p>That is convenient in one way: you cannot end up with two services on incompatible versions of a shared library, and upgrades happen once.</p><p>It is limiting in another: you cannot upgrade a package for one service and leave the others behind, so a risky major version bump has to be validated across everything at once. And every app's image installs packages it does not use.</p><p>This is a real trade-off rather than a defect. If independent versioning matters &mdash; different release cadences, different teams, different risk appetites &mdash; separate repositories or a workspace-based tool with per-package manifests fits better.</p>",
