                  "Summarise Mongoose in NestJS in thirty seconds.",
                solution:
                  "<p>\"<code>forRootAsync</code> for the connection once, <code>forFeature</code> per feature module, <code>@InjectModel</code> to inject &mdash; the same shape as TypeORM, and <code>@InjectModel</code> exists for the same generic-erasure reason.</p><p>Schemas are classes with <code>@Prop</code>, turned into real schemas by <code>SchemaFactory.createForClass</code>; indexes and hooks attach to the <em>schema</em>, after that call.</p><p>The things I watch for: <code>populate</code> is a second query, not a join, so pass a field list and use <code>$lookup</code> for anything heavy; <code>.lean()</code> on read-only queries because hydration is expensive; <code>pre('save')</code> does not fire on <code>updateOne</code>, which is how a password gets stored in plaintext; and updates skip validators unless <code>runValidators</code> is set.</p><p>Aggregation bypasses Mongoose entirely, so ObjectIds must be cast manually or the match silently returns nothing. And <code>autoIndex: false</code> in production, since otherwise every startup rebuilds indexes.\"</p>",
